          "page": 2,
          "y": 246.21,
          "text": "Charles Babbage was an English mathematician, a philosopher and also an inventor. He was born on 1791 in London England. He was known for his contributions to invent machine X to solve four basic arithmetic functions. The machine X has improved its calculations design from Stepped Reckoner machine and early mechanical calculator. The machine X has introduced a number of computing concepts which are still in use today. Although this machine was not actually completed, it is the first machine that deserved to be called as a computer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "page": 2,
          "y": 508.61,
          "text": "a) What is the machine X name?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "page": 2,
          "y": 546.4,
          "text": "b) In which generation does the machine X introduced?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "page": 2,
          "y": 584.56,
          "text": "c) What is the function of machine X?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "page": 2,
          "y": 622.71,
          "text": "d) Name the machine that has been invented prior to machine X?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "page": 2,
          "y": 660.51,
          "text": "e) What is the title given to Charles Babbage due to his success to invent machine X?"
        }
      ]
